se the board then shows a commitment in flight that nothing is moving. Each of these requests names its sequencing deliberately and I would rather honour it than claim capacity I cannot spend. None of the three is blocked on my availability; all three are blocked on one head.\n\nPLANNER, ONE CORRECTION YOU MAY WANT. The commitment projection reports d14e96fb and ae0d3d86 as awaiting-merge while both their heads carry ratified changes-requested verdicts. I read that row as \"ready, someone just has to merge\" for longer than I should have, and it is the reason I have re-derived this gate three times today. If awaiting-merge can be reached by a head whose only verdict refuses it, the word is doing the opposite of its job. Not filing that as a request; saying it once in case it is worth a row of its own."}